  "thumbnailAlt": "Catering Inquiry form beside a photo of elegant catering presentation with gourmet appetizers on a tray at a social event",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A catering inquiry form is a form that collects an event's date, venue, guest count, service style, menu preferences, dietary requirements and budget so a caterer can check availability and send an accurate quote in one reply. This template asks about venue kitchen access, staffing and rentals up front, the details that most often change a catering price after the first quote.",
    "audience": "Caterers, private chefs, food trucks, restaurants with a catering arm, bakeries and event venues that quote for weddings, corporate events and parties.",
    "useCases": [
      "A Get a Quote page on a catering website",
      "Corporate lunch and office party orders from event planners",
      "Wedding catering leads from bridal shows and Instagram",
      "Food truck bookings for festivals and private parties"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Embed the form beside your sample menus with the Split layout so visitors see food and the form together.",
      "Send inquiries to Google Sheets or use webhooks to drop them into your sales pipeline the moment they arrive.",
      "Add the email copy to the respondent so clients have their own event details to check against your quote."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a catering inquiry form include?",
        "answer": "Contact details, event type and date, start time and length, venue name and address, guest count, service style (buffet, plated, family style, canapés, food truck), cuisine or menu ideas, dietary and allergy needs with numbers, whether staff, bar service or rentals are needed, kitchen access at the venue, and a budget per head or total."
      },
      {
        "question": "How far in advance should people book catering?",
        "answer": "Weddings and large events are often booked 6 to 12 months ahead, and corporate events a few weeks ahead. Smaller drop-off orders may need only a few days. Tell clients your own lead time on the form."
      },
      {
        "question": "Why ask for a budget per head?",
        "answer": "A budget lets you suggest a menu and service style that fits, instead of sending a quote that is far too high or too low. Mark it optional if clients are hesitant."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I handle allergies on catering orders?",
        "answer": "Ask for the type of allergy and how many guests have it, then confirm in writing how you will prepare and label those dishes. Follow your local food safety and allergen labeling rules."
      }
    ]
  },
